":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in 4.4.1.stable and 4.5.beta6\n\n### System information\n\nLinux Ubuntu 22.04 - Godot v4.4.1.stable - Vulkan (Forward+)\n\n### Issue description\n\nShapeCast3D sometimes can't detect collision with Trimesh shapes but for Convex shapes it works correctly.\nIn the video, first collision shape is Trimesh and second one is Convex. When player moves under them, shapecast detects edge of the first one but can't detect it in the middle. For Convex it detects collision from start to end.\nBoth Godot Physics and Jolt have this bug but in Godot Physics is less noticeable.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9576e9ab-a2e3-4389-b5e0-7a6b343d8227\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nMRP added and steps described above for the related video.\nEnable \"Visible Collision Shapes\" in debug menu, run project and move player under the boxes.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[JoltShapecastBug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/21932663/JoltShapecastBug.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"mrezai","id":5120436,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMjA0MzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5120436?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrezai","html_url":"https://github.com/mrezai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrezai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrezai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrezai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrezai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrezai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrezai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m